  "status": "published",
  "title": "Canvas and Leather Tote",
  "summary": "Waxed canvas body with riveted leather handles. Carries tools, groceries, or both.",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedHours": 6,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "The finished bag is 15 in wide, 15 in tall and 5 in deep. Cut two 21 x 20 in body panels and one 8 x 7 in pocket from the canvas, marking with chalk. Hold layers with clips, because pins leave permanent holes in waxed canvas.",
    "Cut a 3 in square out of both bottom corners of each panel. With 1/2 in seam allowances this produces the 5 in boxed bottom.",
    "Set up the machine with a 110/18 denim needle and bonded thread top and bobbin, at a 3.5 mm stitch length. Test on a scrap first. Do not touch a hot iron to waxed canvas; finger-press the folds, or use a pressing cloth on low heat.",
    "Hem the pocket's top edge, fold the other edges under 1/2 in, and topstitch it to the inside face of one panel 4 in below the top edge.",
    "Place the panels right sides together and sew the sides and bottom with a 1/2 in seam, backstitching at each end. Zigzag the raw edges.",
    "Box each corner: pull the cut-out open so the side seam sits on the bottom seam, and sew straight across with a 1/2 in seam. Turn the bag right side out.",
    "Fold the top edge 1/2 in and then 1 1/2 in to the inside. Clip it and topstitch close to both folds.",
    "Cut two 22 in handles from the strap. Round the corners, dampen the edges and burnish them with the slicker. Punch two holes in each end, at 1/2 in and 1 1/2 in from the tip. Cut four 1 1/2 in squares from the strap offcut as inside backers.",
    "Position each handle end on the outside 4 in in from a side seam, with the top hole 1/2 in below the bag rim. Punch through the canvas, add a backer inside, and set the rivets on a hard surface with the setter and mallet. Pull hard on each handle to test it before loading the bag."
  ],
